        <rdfs:label>Forward-looking MAE Standard - &quot;Would&quot; Language</rdfs:label>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="es-es">Estándar de MAE con miras al futuro - Lenguaje &quot;Would&quot;</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="es-mx">Estándar de MAE con miras al futuro - Lenguaje &quot;Would&quot;</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="de-de">Forward-Looking MAE-Standard - &quot;Würde&quot;-Sprache</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en-gb">Forward-looking MAE Standard - &quot;Would&quot; Language</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="fr-fr">Norme MAE prospective - Langage &quot;Would&quot;</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="pt-br">Padrão MAE de olhar para frente - Linguagem &quot;Would&quot;</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="he-il">תקן MAE המתבסס על תפיסת העתיד - שפת &quot;Would&quot;</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="hi-in">फॉरवर्ड-लुकिंग एमएई मानक - &quot;Would&quot; भाषा</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="zh-cn">前瞻性 MAE 标准 - &quot;Would&quot; 语言</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="ja-jp">将来志向的MAE標準 - &quot;Would&quot;言語</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:definition>A Forward-looking MAE Standard with &quot;Would&quot; Language is a legal concept that refers to a standard used in contracts to determine whether a material adverse effect has occurred, where the standard is based on whether the effect would reasonably be expected to occur in the future.</skos:definition>
    </owl:Class>
    


