        <rdfs:label>Exchange Visitor Visa</rdfs:label>
        <skos:altLabel>A Cultural/Educational Exchange Visa is a non-immigrant visa issued to participants in programs that promote cultural exchange, primarily for studying, teaching, research, or training. In the United States, it&apos;s called a J-1 Visa, allowing the holder to stay temporarily in the host country, and they may be subject to a two-year home-country physical presence requirement upon completion of their program.</skos:altLabel>
