        <skos:altLabel>Deceased Individual</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:definition>A decedent is a legal term used to refer to a deceased person, particularly in the context of estate planning and probate law. The decedent&apos;s estate encompasses all assets, liabilities, rights, and obligations left behind, which are subject to administration and distribution according to the decedent&apos;s will or state intestacy laws.</skos:definition>
