        <skos:altLabel>Meat Cattle</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:definition>Beef Cattle are domesticated bovine animals bred and raised primarily for meat production. These cattle are known for their muscular build, efficient growth rates, and significant role in the agricultural industry, providing high-quality beef for consumption.</skos:definition>
