        <skos:definition>U.S. Legislative Branch, known as Congress, is the federal government&apos;s law-making body, responsible for drafting, debating, and passing legislation. It is a bicameral institution consisting of the Senate and the House of Representatives, each with distinct roles and responsibilities.</skos:definition>
        <skos:prefLabel>Congress</skos:prefLabel>
    </owl:Class>
    


