        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:label>Trust and Estate Claims</rdfs:label>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="de-de">Ansprüche aus Treuhand- und Nachlassangelegenheiten</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="pt-br">Reivindicações de confiança e patrimônio</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="fr-fr">Réclamations en matière de fiducie et de succession</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="zh-cn">信托和遗产索赔</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="ja-jp">信託および相続請求</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:definition>Trust and Estate Claims refer to legal actions related to disputes over the distribution of assets and property left behind by a deceased person, including challenges to the validity of wills, allegations of mismanagement by trustees, and interference with expected inheritances.</skos:definition>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/R3SsfeWPlXfVmWY2C1XmXf -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/R3SsfeWPlXfVmWY2C1XmXf">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RCzxVprwB3RwZ8EMewt18Jt"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RcPmc5tXDkOmcv3W8TxwTO"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#seeAlso"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RUhSbbDJZa8Crs3tIWcIfV"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#seeAlso"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/pYi9zljbSU6w62eKekO9CQ"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:label>Real Estate Investment Trust</rdfs:label>
        <skos:definition>A Real Estate Investment Trust (REIT) is a company that owns, operates, or finances income-producing real estate, and allows individual investors to buy shares in residential, commercial, and industrial properties.</skos:definition>
        <skos:prefLabel>REIT</skos:prefLabel>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/R3SySoBpqTLFk1SEcLT3cw -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/R3SySoBpqTLFk1SEcLT3cw">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RsaC1DeVmdIpw8YKXA9JNt"/>
        <rdfs:label>Split-off</rdfs:label>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="de-de">Abspaltung</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="pt-br">Cisão</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="es-es">Escisión</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="fr-fr">Scission</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="es-mx">Separación</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en-gb">Split-off</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="he-il">פיצול</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="hi-in">विभाजन</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="zh-cn">分拆</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="ja-jp">分社化</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:definition>A split-off divestiture is a corporate action in which a company separates a business unit, division, or subsidiary into a standalone, independent entity, but unlike a spin-off, it requires existing shareholders to exchange their shares in the parent company for shares in the newly formed entity. This process effectively separates the ownership of the parent company and the newly created company. Split-off divestitures are undertaken for various reasons, such as to focus on core competencies, improve operational efficiency, or comply with regulatory requirements.</skos:definition>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/R3T71xF5Wg0o0uZpVyLwF4 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/R3T71xF5Wg0o0uZpVyLwF4">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/R7pZSuLowh1QRBeGOhk6zEr"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RBdzXlcak91MmI7U2nHYMU"/>
        <rdfs:label>Motion to Extend Time to File Reply</rdfs:label>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="de-de">Antrag auf Verlängerung der Frist zur Einreichung einer Erwiderung</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="es-mx">Moción para extender el plazo para presentar la réplica</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en-gb">Motion to Extend Time to File Reply</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="pt-br">Petição para prorrogar o prazo para apresentação de resposta</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="fr-fr">Requête en vue de proroger le délai de dépôt d&apos;une réponse</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="es-es">Solicitud de prórroga de plazo para presentar la réplica</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="he-il">תנועה להארכת הזמן להגשת תשובה</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="hi-in">जवाब देने के लिए समय बढ़ाने की मोशन</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="zh-cn">延长答复期限动议</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="ja-jp">返答期限延長申立書</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:definition>A Motion to Extend Time to File Reply is a formal request made to a court, either appellate or trial, to grant additional time beyond the original deadline for a party to submit a reply brief or response.</skos:definition>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/R3TYUV6LmKIQOgoryLdAbc -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/R3TYUV6LmKIQOgoryLdAbc">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/R9Ii4OzSADsjS0VegX12oQJ"/>
        <rdfs:label>Motion to Determine Tax Liability</rdfs:label>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="de-de">Antrag auf Feststellung der Steuerhaftung</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="es-mx">Moción para determinar la responsabilidad fiscal</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="es-es">Moción para determinar la responsabilidad tributaria</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en-gb">Motion to Determine Tax Liability</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="pt-br">Petição para Determinação da Responsabilidade Tributária</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="fr-fr">Requête en vue de déterminer la responsabilité fiscale</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="he-il">תביעה לקביעת אחריות מס</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="hi-in">कर दायित्व निर्धारित करने के लिए याचिका</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="zh-cn">确定税务责任动议</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="ja-jp">課税責任の決定を求める請願</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:definition>A Motion to Determine Tax Liability is a legal request made in a bankruptcy case to determine the amount of taxes owed by the debtor.</skos:definition>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/R3TZludg4KJtTjPW1T2J9c -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/R3TZludg4KJtTjPW1T2J9c">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/R8N4pMIOhTNbqcmDczSephq"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#seeAlso"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/R79rOnHd0QSHnD78a0WUK1J"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#seeAlso"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/R86jPmGuwTs8kyeJw0atFjh"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:label>Visa Waived</rdfs:label>
        <skos:altLabel>VWP</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel>Visa Waiver</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:definition>The Visa Waiver Program (VWP) allows citizens of participating countries to travel to the destination country for tourism or business purposes without obtaining a visa. In the United States, travel under the VWP is permitted for up to 90 days and does not allow for a change of status or an extension of stay</skos:definition>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/R3TtiS3gxiA1y6P4bIeoRl -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/R3TtiS3gxiA1y6P4bIeoRl">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/R8DuEmmnbcptnIZhPdF2Tvx"/>
        <rdfs:isDefinedBy>From LEDES (Legal Electronic Data Exchange Standard). https://ledes.org/</rdfs:isDefinedBy>
        <rdfs:label>Fee Credit Note</rdfs:label>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en-gb">Fee Credit Note</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="de-de">Gutschrift</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="pt-br">Nota de crédito</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="es-es">Nota de crédito de tarifa</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="es-mx">Nota de crédito de tarifa</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="fr-fr">Note de crédit</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="he-il">כתב זיכוי עמלה</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="hi-in">फी क्रेडिट नोट</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="ja-jp">請求書クレジットノート</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="zh-cn">费用贷项通知单</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:definition>A Fee Credit Note is a type of discount or credit given to a client by a legal service provider, typically applied to future legal fees owed by the client.</skos:definition>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/R3UaBbDJ6SxaH8wmyQqQw0g -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/R3UaBbDJ6SxaH8wmyQqQw0g">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RtpnOBk4lRnWigpEBBKYUDQ"/>
        <rdfs:label>X111 Online Legal Research</rdfs:label>
        <skos:definition>Any electronic legal research service charges, such as for LexisNexis or Westlaw</skos:definition>
        <skos:prefLabel>X111 Online Legal Research</skos:prefLabel>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/R3UxGY4BMNFrNvdJBDDT6I -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/R3UxGY4BMNFrNvdJBDDT6I">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RuliWeVDE8CQi4AATMNab1"/>
        <rdfs:label>Pullman Abstention</rdfs:label>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="es-es">Abstención de Pullman</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="es-mx">Abstención de Pullman</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="fr-fr">Abstention de Pullman</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="pt-br">Abstenção de Pullman</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en-gb">Pullman Abstention</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="de-de">Pullman-Abstinenz</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="he-il">פולמן נימול</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="hi-in">पुलमैन अवहेलना</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="ja-jp">プルマン棄権</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="zh-cn">普尔曼回避原则</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:definition>A legal doctrine known as Pullman Abstention allows a federal court to abstain from hearing a case that involves a state law that is unclear or unsettled, in order to allow the state court to clarify the law and avoid unnecessary federal constitutional issues.</skos:definition>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/R3VixBhxprWbjrMlnVJ26w -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/R3VixBhxprWbjrMlnVJ26w">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/R9Ii4OzSADsjS0VegX12oQJ"/>
        <rdfs:label>Motion for Production of Documents</rdfs:label>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="de-de">Antrag auf Vorlage von Dokumenten</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="es-mx">Moción para la producción de documentos</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en-gb">Motion for Production of Documents</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="pt-br">Pedido de Produção de Documentos</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="fr-fr">Requête en production de documents</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="es-es">Solicitud de producción de documentos</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="he-il">תביעה להפקת מסמכים</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="hi-in">दस्तावेज़ों के उत्पादन के लिए मोशन</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="zh-cn">提交文件生产动议</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="ja-jp">書類開示請求</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:definition>A Motion for Production of Documents is a formal request made in a bankruptcy case for the opposing party to provide specific documents or evidence relevant to the case.</skos:definition>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/R3Vk2eHOjTsqOyQaAHjVFIg -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/R3Vk2eHOjTsqOyQaAHjVFIg">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RnTEPb_LCSNqAkQqrfte8zg"/>
        <rdfs:label>A125 Document Production Creation and Preparation</rdfs:label>
        <skos:definition>For discovery and eDiscovery, the creation, export or delivery of a document production set including: creation of production export, metadata redaction, creation of delivery media and image branding. Excludes cost of printed set (X101 or X102).</skos:definition>
        <skos:prefLabel>A125 Document Production Creation and Preparation</skos:prefLabel>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/R3Xgl77xYQjGnw8EJTT7gn -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/R3Xgl77xYQjGnw8EJTT7gn">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RXwl9xfFnpmQn8Ex816ROD"/>
        <rdfs:label>Client Organizational Unit</rdfs:label>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en-gb">Client Organisational Unit</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="de-de">Kundenorganisationsbereich</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="es-es">Unidad Organizativa del Cliente</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="es-mx">Unidad Organizativa del Cliente</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="pt-br">Unidade organizacional do cliente</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="fr-fr">Unité organisationnelle client</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="he-il">יחידת ארגון לקוח</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="hi-in">ग्राहक संगठनिक इकाई</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="ja-jp">クライアント組織単位</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="zh-cn">客户组织单位</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:definition>The particular company entity/division/unit (e.g., Sales, Human Resources) for which the legal work is being performed.</skos:definition>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/R3XhsEnunIrdi5MYNdLqGL -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/R3XhsEnunIrdi5MYNdLqGL">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RBJlYzE4ZY14dTEghzbbMHg"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#seeAlso"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/R4YBBDxkx2m0Iy4bgKxjz1"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#seeAlso"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/R9luHEuui2taMrChZ8b08sd"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#seeAlso"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RE4D96703A56bF283055585d"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#seeAlso"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RZ8wDdA7ASzGtn9sVWS3Si"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:label>Children&apos;s Rights</rdfs:label>
        <skos:definition>Children&apos;s rights are the legal and moral entitlements specifically aimed at the protection and welfare of minors. These rights may include, but are not limited to, the right to education, healthcare, protection from abuse and exploitation, and participation in family and cultural life, often upheld by international law such as the United Nations Convention on the Rights of the Child.</skos:definition>
        <skos:prefLabel>Rights of the Child</skos:prefLabel>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/R3XuZ2VcNStGsIrlegqW_-g -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/R3XuZ2VcNStGsIrlegqW_-g">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/R_SzQ5B5tSJymAiew37taiw"/>
        <rdfs:label>WC180 Alternative Fee Arrangements</rdfs:label>
        <skos:definition>This code includes all non-hourly or other alternative fee arrangements for tasks and activities in this phase.</skos:definition>
        <skos:prefLabel>WC180 Alternative Fee Arrangements</skos:prefLabel>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/R3a93_SRkRRS5rksR9Xy1IQ -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/R3a93_SRkRRS5rksR9Xy1IQ">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RbFgivFxOQ5aR8Vwh9-rvVw"/>
        <rdfs:label>TR400 Domestic Trademark Prosecution and Renewal</rdfs:label>
        <skos:definition>All action associated with prosecuting and renewing a trademark application in the home country of an applicant, including initial review and any calendaring of any response deadline, report to client with any proposed response, review of applicant&apos;s instructions and comments, preparation of amendments and/or responsive arguments, examiner interviews, and report of actions to the client. Excludes any filings in response to Official Communications under TR430. Includes any affidavit, petition, extension, declaration and other requests for supervisory action that are not decided by a quasi-judicial or appellate tribunal within the Trademark Office. Note that governmental fees and external expenses (or &quot;disbursements&quot; in the US) are included under E100.</skos:definition>
        <skos:prefLabel>TR400 Domestic Trademark Prosecution and Renewal</skos:prefLabel>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/R3b7f27oh98hVpr5wWvYes -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/R3b7f27oh98hVpr5wWvYes">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RDF3VrmH1eapfkrSQstevLs"/>
        <dc:source rdf:resource="https://www.ssa.gov/disability/professionals/bluebook/13.00-NeoplasticDiseases-Malignant-Adult.htm#13_19"/>
        <rdfs:label>Liver or Gallbladder Cancer</rdfs:label>
        <skos:altLabel>Gallbladder Cancer</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel>Hepatic Cancer</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel>Hepatic Carcinoma</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel>Liver Carcinoma</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:definition>Liver cancer is a type of cancer that originates in the liver cells, with the most common type being hepatocellular carcinoma. It often requires treatments such as surgery, chemotherapy, radiation therapy, and targeted therapy, depending on the stage and extent of the disease.</skos:definition>
        <skos:prefLabel>Liver Cancer</skos:prefLabel>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/R3bU74bKrSAyu2rkZ4SZEa -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/R3bU74bKrSAyu2rkZ4SZEa">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RCUqAm74lUE8pmrNqTadcrl"/>
        <rdfs:label>Negative Covenant</rdfs:label>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="fr-fr">Convention négative</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="pt-br">Covenants negativos</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="es-es">Covenio Negativo</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="es-mx">Covenio Negativo</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en-gb">Negative Covenant</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="de-de">Negativer Vertrag</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="he-il">הבטחת חובת חריגה</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="hi-in">नकारात्मक शपथ</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="ja-jp">ネガティブ・カバナント</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="zh-cn">负面契约</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:definition>A Negative Covenant is a legal provision that prohibits a party from performing a certain action or engaging in a particular activity, as specified in a contract or agreement.</skos:definition>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/R3e2z0YyuTWB0E6NALitBX -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/R3e2z0YyuTWB0E6NALitBX">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RDSBerlLWg1ntpLqDQn1eVn"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#seeAlso"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RDumnatrYH4kRxr787bJf4R"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:label>Abandonment of Property</rdfs:label>
        <skos:altLabel>Bona Vacantia</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel>Property Forfeiture</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel>Reversion to the State</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel>Unclaimed Property Transfer</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:definition>Escheatment is the legal process by which unclaimed or abandoned property reverts to the state. This occurs when the rightful owner of the property cannot be located or has failed to claim ownership within a specified period, resulting in the transfer of the property to government custody.</skos:definition>
        <skos:prefLabel>Escheatment</skos:prefLabel>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/R3erD0I2JnRN8fVHGUfFoq -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/R3erD0I2JnRN8fVHGUfFoq">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/R73Uo5x4VyfiOXt6i4R256t"/>
        <rdfs:label>Prehearing Conference</rdfs:label>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="es-es">Conferencia previa a la audiencia</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="es-mx">Conferencia previa a la audiencia</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="pt-br">Conferência prévia</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="fr-fr">Conférence préliminaire</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en-gb">Prehearing Conference</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="de-de">Vorverhandlungskonferenz</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="he-il">כנס ראשוני לפני הדיון</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="hi-in">प्रारंभिक सुनवाई सम्मेलन</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="ja-jp">事前審問会議</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="zh-cn">庭前会议</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:definition>A Prehearing Conference is a litigation event that occurs before a hearing, where the parties and the judge discuss the case and attempt to resolve any issues or streamline the hearing process.</skos:definition>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/R3gxP7qFBBfoVwuD03aMOt -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/R3gxP7qFBBfoVwuD03aMOt">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/R9q7GJc1zsYT0P4Xdp6l9Oz"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#seeAlso"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RCpnqQCzeexk3k9kkbLx1Zu"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:label>Judicial Discretion</rdfs:label>
        <skos:definition>Judicial discretion refers to the power and authority granted to judges to make decisions or take actions within the bounds of the law based on their interpretation, judgment, and application of legal principles. This discretion is exercised to ensure justice and fairness but is generally subject to appellate review to prevent arbitrary or capricious rulings.</skos:definition>
    </owl:Class>
    


