        <rdfs:label>Bankruptcy Schedule - Executory Contracts and Unexpired Leases</rdfs:label>
        <skos:altLabel>Active Leases Schedule</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel>Executory Agreements List</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel>Ongoing Agreements Disclosure</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel>Ongoing Contracts Schedule</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:definition>Bankruptcy Schedule - Executory Contracts and Unexpired Leases, also known as Schedule G, requires the debtor to list all ongoing contracts and active leases that have not been fully performed or expired as of the bankruptcy filing date. This schedule provides details about each contract and lease, including the counterparty&apos;s name, the nature of the agreement, and any relevant terms.</skos:definition>
        <skos:prefLabel>Schedule G</skos:prefLabel>
    </owl:Class>
    


