        <skos:definition>The Centers for Medicare &amp; Medicaid Services (CMS), previously known as the Health Care Financing Administration (HCFA), is a federal agency within the United States Department of Health and Human Services (HHS) that administers the Medicare program and works in partnership with state governments to administer Medicaid, the Children&apos;s Health Insurance Program (CHIP), and health insurance portability standards.</skos:definition>
