        <dc:identifier>US-FD-TREAS-IRS-APPEALS</dc:identifier>
        <rdfs:label>IRS Office of Appeals</rdfs:label>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="fr-fr">Bureau des appels de l&apos;IRS</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="pt-br">Escritório de Recursos do IRS</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en-gb">IRS Office of Appeals</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="de-de">IRS-Berufungsbüro</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="ja-jp">IRS控訴局</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="es-es">Oficina de Apelaciones del IRS</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="es-mx">Oficina de Apelaciones del IRS</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="he-il">משרד הערעורים של ה-IRS</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="hi-in">आयकर विभाग की अपील कार्यालय</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="zh-cn">美国国税局上诉办公室</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:definition>The IRS Office of Appeals is an independent organization within the IRS that helps taxpayers resolve their tax disputes through an informal, administrative process. Our mission is to resolve tax controversies fairly and impartially, without litigation. Appeals reviews cases after the IRS has made its decision, offering an objective point of view on each appealed case.</skos:definition>
