        <skos:definition>Cranberries are small, tart berries from the Vaccinium genus, primarily grown in cool, temperate regions. They are commonly consumed as juice, sauces, and dried snacks, and are valued for their high vitamin C and antioxidant content, as well as their health benefits, particularly in urinary tract health.</skos:definition>
    </owl:Class>
    


