        <rdfs:label>Native Alaskan</rdfs:label>
        <skos:definition>A Native Alaskan is an indigenous person originating from Alaska, often belonging to groups such as the Inuit, Yupik, Aleut, or various Native American tribes. Native Alaskans have distinct cultures, languages, and traditions, and they are recognized as the original inhabitants of the Alaska region</skos:definition>
