        <skos:definition>A Stipulated Voluntary Dismissal without Prejudice is a legal agreement between parties in a lawsuit where the plaintiff agrees to dismiss the case voluntarily, without prejudice, meaning that they can refile the case in the future if necessary.</skos:definition>
