        <skos:altLabel>Specialty Occupation Visa</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:definition>A Specialty Occupation Visa is a type of visa that allows foreign nationals to work in a job that requires specialized knowledge or expertise, typically at a professional level that requires at least a bachelor&apos;s degree or equivalent. This visa category is often designed to address specific labor shortages or to attract individuals with specialized skills to contribute to a country&apos;s economy.</skos:definition>
        <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en-us">H-1B Visa</skos:prefLabel>
    </owl:Class>
    


