        <rdfs:label>U.S. Dept. of Housing and Urban Development</rdfs:label>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="pt-br">Departamento de Habitação e Desenvolvimento Urbano dos EUA</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="es-es">Departamento de Vivienda y Desarrollo Urbano de EE. UU.</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="es-mx">Departamento de Vivienda y Desarrollo Urbano de EE. UU.</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="fr-fr">Département du logement et du développement urbain des États-Unis</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en-gb">U.S. Dept. of Housing and Urban Development</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="de-de">US-amerikanisches Ministerium für Wohnungsbau und Stadtentwicklung</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="he-il">משרד המגורים ופיתוח העירוני של ארצות הברית</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="hi-in">यूएस आवास और शहरी विकास विभाग</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="ja-jp">米国住宅都市開発省</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="zh-cn">美国住房和城市发展部</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:definition>The United States Department of Housing and Urban Development (HUD) is a Cabinet department in the Executive branch of the United States federal government. HUD&apos;s mission is to create strong, sustainable, inclusive communities and quality affordable homes for all. HUD is working to strengthen the housing market to bolster the economy and protect consumers; meet the need for quality affordable rental homes; utilize housing as a platform for improving quality of life; build inclusive and sustainable communities free from discrimination, and transform the way HUD does business.</skos:definition>
        <skos:hiddenLabel>HUD</skos:hiddenLabel>
        <skos:prefLabel>Department of Housing and Urban Development</skos:prefLabel>
    </owl:Class>
    


