        <skos:altLabel>Loan Interest Payment</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:definition>An Interest Payment is a periodic payment made by a borrower to a lender as compensation for the use of borrowed funds. This payment is typically a percentage of the principal amount and is agreed upon at the time of the loan agreement, representing the cost of borrowing money.</skos:definition>
