        <rdfs:label>Visa Priority Date</rdfs:label>
        <skos:altLabel>Queue Date</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:definition>The immigration priority date is a critical concept in immigration system, marking the date when an individual&apos;s application for a visa or permanent residency (such as filing Form I-485) is first received by the relevant authority. This date determines the applicant&apos;s place in the queue for visa availability, as visas are allocated based on the priority date in conjunction with the visa bulletin.</skos:definition>
        <skos:prefLabel>Immigration Priority Date</skos:prefLabel>
    </owl:Class>
    


