        <dc:source rdf:resource="https://www.ssa.gov/disability/professionals/bluebook/9.00-Endocrine-Adult.htm"/>
        <rdfs:label>Hypoglycemia</rdfs:label>
        <skos:altLabel>Low Blood Glucose</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:definition>Hypoglycemia is an abnormally low level of blood glucose, which can result from diabetes management or other conditions. Symptoms can be recognized and reversed by consuming glucose-containing substances, though some individuals may not recognize the symptoms due to hypoglycemia unawareness. Severe cases can lead to complications like seizures or loss of consciousness.</skos:definition>
        <skos:prefLabel>Low Blood Sugar</skos:prefLabel>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/R7TLlJ71b9UaOSriKDsUnEd -->

