        <skos:definition>Legislative drafting practice involves the creation of legal texts that are intended to become laws, typically performed by specialized legal experts or legislative counsel. This practice requires a deep understanding of legal principles, legislative processes, and the ability to write clearly and unambiguously, with the goal of producing enforceable and effective laws.</skos:definition>
