        <skos:altLabel>Blood Cancer</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel>Hematologic Cancer</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:definition>Leukemia is a type of cancer that affects the blood and bone marrow, characterized by the overproduction of abnormal white blood cells. This disease can be acute or chronic and often requires treatments such as chemotherapy, radiation therapy, or stem cell transplantation.</skos:definition>
