        <rdfs:label>Mosaic Down Syndrome</rdfs:label>
        <skos:altLabel>Mosaic Trisomy 21</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:definition>Mosaic Down syndrome is a genetic condition in which an individual has a mixture of cells, some with the usual two copies of chromosome 21 and others with three copies (trisomy 21). This results in a mosaic pattern of normal and abnormal cells.</skos:definition>
    </owl:Class>
    


