        <rdfs:label>Public Housing Benefit</rdfs:label>
        <skos:altLabel>Public Housing</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:definition>Housing public benefit programs refer to government initiatives that provide assistance to individuals or families in obtaining affordable and safe housing. These programs often include subsidies, vouchers, or direct assistance to help low-income or vulnerable populations access housing that meets their needs. The specific eligibility criteria, types of assistance, and regulations governing such programs can vary widely by jurisdiction.</skos:definition>
        <skos:prefLabel>Subsidized Housing</skos:prefLabel>
    </owl:Class>
    


