        <skos:altLabel>Exclusion from Inheritance</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel>Heir Exclusion</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:definition>Disinheritance is the legal act of deliberately excluding an heir from receiving property or assets from a deceased person&apos;s estate, typically through the terms specified in a will or trust. This action can be taken for various personal, financial, or relational reasons, and must comply with legal statutes to be effective.</skos:definition>
        <skos:prefLabel>Disownment</skos:prefLabel>
    </owl:Class>
    


