        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#seeAlso"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RcTA2iQmrtqOnX3WrjJIp8"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:label>Contact Name Suffix - J.D. (Juris Doctor)</rdfs:label>
        <skos:altLabel>Esq.</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel>Esquire</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel>Juris Doctor</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:definition>The suffix &quot;J.D.&quot; stands for &quot;Juris Doctor&quot; and is used after a person&apos;s name to signify that they have earned the professional graduate degree in law. This designation indicates the individual&apos;s qualifications to practice law in a particular jurisdiction, provided they have passed the bar exam, and is commonly used in legal settings, academic environments, and formal documents.</skos:definition>
        <skos:prefLabel>J.D.</skos:prefLabel>
    </owl:Class>
    


