        <skos:definition>A pension account is a financial arrangement where an individual or employee contributes funds during their working years to build a retirement fund. The accumulated funds are invested, and upon retirement, the account provides regular payments or a lump sum to support the retiree&apos;s financial needs.</skos:definition>
    </owl:Class>
    


