        <skos:definition>An Uncontested Adoption is when all relevant parties agree on the adoption of a child without any opposition. Typically, the biological parents have either voluntarily relinquished their parental rights or have had them legally terminated, allowing the adoption process to proceed smoothly and without legal disputes.</skos:definition>
    </owl:Class>
    


