        <skos:definition>Bankruptcy Plan Consummation refers to the completion of the necessary actions outlined in a bankruptcy plan, leading to its implementation. It marks the point at which the bankruptcy proceedings are consummated, and the plan&apos;s terms are effectuated.</skos:definition>
