        <rdfs:label>Turkeys</rdfs:label>
        <skos:definition>Turkeys are large domesticated birds belonging to the species Meleagris gallopavo, commonly raised for their meat. Known for their distinctive fan-shaped tail and wattled neck, turkeys are an important source of poultry, particularly in North America, where they play a central role in traditional meals like Thanksgiving.</skos:definition>
    </owl:Class>
    


