        <skos:altLabel>Social Assistance Benefit</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel>Tax-Funded Benefit</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:definition>A type of social security benefit funded by general tax revenues rather than individual contributions, typically provided to eligible individuals based on criteria such as age, disability, or income level. Non-contributory benefits aim to provide a basic level of social protection and poverty alleviation for those who may not have contributed sufficiently to qualify for contributory benefits.</skos:definition>
    </owl:Class>
    


