        <skos:definition>A Motion in Limine to Exclude Hearsay Witness is a legal request made by one party to prevent the other party from presenting testimony from a witness who will testify about statements made by someone else out of court, which are being offered to prove the truth of the matter asserted.</skos:definition>
    </owl:Class>
    


