        <rdfs:label>Service Animals</rdfs:label>
        <skos:altLabel>Assistance Animal</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel>Helper Animal</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel>Support Animal</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:definition>A Service Animal is a specially trained animal that performs tasks or provides assistance to individuals with disabilities, enhancing their ability to perform daily activities. These animals are typically trained to support physical, sensory, psychiatric, or intellectual disabilities and are legally recognized to accompany their handlers in most public places.</skos:definition>
    </owl:Class>
    


