        <skos:altLabel>Court-Ordered Damages Decrease</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel>Decreased Damages Award</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel>Judicial Reduction In Damages</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:definition>Remittitur refers to a court&apos;s power to reduce the amount of damages awarded by a jury if the judge finds the award excessive. This practice is used to prevent the need for a new trial by offering the plaintiff the option to accept a lower amount.</skos:definition>
    </owl:Class>
    


