            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:label>Good Standing Certificate</rdfs:label>
        <skos:definition>A Good Standing Certificate is a legal document issued by a governmental authority or a regulatory body, certifying that a corporation, limited liability company, or other legal entity is registered, active, and in compliance with state or jurisdictional requirements. It indicates that the entity has fulfilled its obligations, such as filing annual reports and paying necessary fees, and is authorized to conduct business.</skos:definition>
        <skos:prefLabel>Certificate of Good Standing</skos:prefLabel>
    </owl:Class>
    


