        <skos:altLabel>Cerebral Death</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:definition>Brain death is a medical and legal condition characterized by the irreversible cessation of all brain functions, including those of the brain stem. It can be legally recognized as the end of life, and it has significant implications for organ donation, end-of-life care, and the determination of the time of death.</skos:definition>
