        <rdfs:label>Judicial Clerk</rdfs:label>
        <skos:altLabel>Court Clerk</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:definition>A Judicial Clerk is a legal professional, typically a recent law school graduate, who assists a judge with research, writing opinions, and other tasks essential to judicial proceedings. Judicial clerks play a critical role in the judicial process by providing detailed analysis and support for the judge&apos;s decision-making.</skos:definition>
