        <skos:definition>A Stipulation to Avoid Lien is a legal agreement between parties that prevents a lien from being placed on a property or asset.</skos:definition>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/R8HB6Mavva8opxRpynzNOcH -->

