        <skos:definition>A Living Trust, also known as a revocable trust, is a legal entity created during the grantor&apos;s lifetime to hold and manage assets. It can be altered, amended, or revoked by the grantor at any time before their death, allowing flexibility in asset management and distribution.</skos:definition>
