        <skos:altLabel>Local Legislative Representative</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel>Municipal Official</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel>Town Official</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:definition>A Local Governmental Leader is an elected or appointed official who holds a position of authority in a municipal or regional government body. This individual is responsible for making decisions, implementing policies, and representing the interests of their constituents within a specific geographic area smaller than a state or province.</skos:definition>
