        <skos:definition>Work Allocation Management refers to the process of assigning and distributing tasks and responsibilities among legal professionals within a law firm or legal department, as part of the overall management of legal operations and business activities.</skos:definition>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/R8OmVstIMR7qzYcAWgAkhmn -->

