        <rdfs:label>Not Guilty</rdfs:label>
        <skos:definition>&quot;Not guilty&quot; is a legal determination made by a court in a criminal case when the defendant has been acquitted or found not responsible for the charges brought against them. It indicates that the prosecution failed to prove the defendant&apos;s guilt, and as a result, the defendant is not subject to criminal penalties or convictions for the alleged crime.</skos:definition>
