        <skos:definition>An Asynchronous Broadcast Transmission, also known as a &quot;Pre-Recorded Broadcast,&quot; is the dissemination of audio and/or video content that has been recorded prior to its scheduled broadcast time. This form of broadcasting includes pre-recorded TV shows, radio programs, and other content that is not transmitted live but is played back at a designated time.</skos:definition>
