        <rdfs:label>Turnips</rdfs:label>
        <skos:altLabel>Brassica Rapa</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:definition>Turnips are root vegetables belonging to the Brassica rapa species, characterized by their round or elongated shape with a white or purple skin and white flesh. They are cultivated for their edible taproot and leaves, both of which are used in various culinary applications and are valued for their nutritional content and storage capabilities.</skos:definition>
