        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="ja-jp">排除権</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:definition>A peremptory challenge is a motion made during a trial to remove a potential juror or judge without stating a reason, typically limited in number, and used to ensure a fair and impartial trial.</skos:definition>
