        <skos:altLabel>Airport Land Asset</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel>Aviation Real Estate</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:definition>An Airport - Real Estate Asset refers to the land, buildings, and infrastructure associated with an airport, including runways, terminals, and other facilities. This type of asset involves both operational and non-operational properties that contribute to the airport&apos;s functionality and revenue generation.</skos:definition>
        <skos:example>An investment group purchases an airport hangar as part of its aviation real estate portfolio.</skos:example>
        <skos:prefLabel>Airport Property</skos:prefLabel>
    </owl:Class>
    


