            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:label>L310 Written Discovery</rdfs:label>
        <skos:definition>L310 Written Discovery refers to the process of obtaining information from the opposing party through written requests, such as interrogatories, requests for admission, and requests for production of documents, as part of the broader legal process of discovery.</skos:definition>
    </owl:Class>
    


