        <rdfs:comment>From LIST: Legal Issues Taxonomy — https://taxonomy.legal/</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Regulatory Exemption</rdfs:label>
        <skos:definition>Regulatory exemption refers to a provision that allows an individual, business, or activity to be excused from complying with certain rules or requirements typically imposed by a regulatory authority. Exemptions are usually granted to promote specific policy objectives or because the standard regulations are deemed unnecessary or overly burdensome in particular cases.</skos:definition>
    </owl:Class>
    


