        <skos:definition>Private Fund Reporting Form (in the U.S., Form PF) is a regulatory filing required by the regulatory authority (e.g., U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission (SEC)) for private fund advisers managing hedge funds and other private funds, providing detailed information about their activities and assets under management. In the U.S., this form aims to assist the Financial Stability Oversight Council (FSOC) in monitoring systemic risk in the financial markets.</skos:definition>
        <skos:prefLabel>Form PF</skos:prefLabel>
    </owl:Class>
    


