        <rdfs:label>Multinational Market Regions</rdfs:label>
        <skos:definition>Multinational Market Regions refer to large geographical areas that encompass multiple countries and are often used for business, economic, and marketing purposes to group markets with similar economic, cultural, or regulatory characteristics. Examples include Latin America, EMEA (Europe, Middle East, and Africa), and APAC (Asia-Pacific).</skos:definition>
    </owl:Class>
    


