        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="zh-cn">缩短的寿命期限</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:definition>Reduced Life Expectancy: A type of non-economic damages in a legal matter where the plaintiff&apos;s life expectancy is shortened due to the defendant&apos;s actions or negligence.</skos:definition>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/R9FMAbfEYARhk9Z0a5Fvij1 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/R9FMAbfEYARhk9Z0a5Fvij1">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RbvEeHm8jkxY6SgfxEoC0i"/>
        <rdfs:label>Fractional Ownership Assets</rdfs:label>
        <skos:definition>Fractional Ownership Assets, such as timeshares, are assets that are owned by multiple individuals or entities, each holding a fraction of the ownership and entitled to use or benefit from the asset for a specific period. In the case of timeshares, owners typically have the right to use a vacation property for a set number of weeks each year, while sharing the costs and responsibilities of ownership and maintenance.</skos:definition>
    </owl:Class>
    


