        <rdfs:label>Trust</rdfs:label>
        <skos:definition>A trust, in estate planning, is a legal entity that holds and manages assets for the benefit of specific individuals or entities, known as beneficiaries. It&apos;s established by a grantor (or settlor) and is overseen by a trustee who ensures the assets are managed and distributed according to the grantor&apos;s instructions.</skos:definition>
    </owl:Class>
    


