        <rdfs:label>Factoring Agreement</rdfs:label>
        <skos:definition>A Factoring Agreement is a financial arrangement where a business sells its accounts receivable, or invoices, to a third-party factoring company at a discount. This agreement outlines the terms and conditions under which the factoring company will advance funds, collect payments, and charge fees, providing immediate liquidity to the original business.</skos:definition>
    </owl:Class>
    


