        <skos:definition>Dementia is a broad category of brain diseases characterized by a decline in memory, thinking, behavior, and the ability to perform everyday activities. It is a progressive condition that often leads to significant impairment in social and occupational functioning, requiring comprehensive medical and supportive care.</skos:definition>
    </owl:Class>
    


