        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="zh-cn">争议金额 - 表示为“最高”</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:definition>The maximum amount in controversy, where the actual amount in dispute is below that maximum. Example: Small-claims courts (also known as &quot;conciliation courts&quot; frequently have a maximum amount of controversy (e.g., $1,000 or $10,000) — over which the case must be argued in a higher court (e.g., state district court).</skos:definition>
    </owl:Class>
    


