        <rdfs:label>Fiber Evidence</rdfs:label>
        <skos:definition>Fiber evidence comprises tiny threads or fragments from textiles found at crime scenes or on objects. Forensic analysis can determine the type, source, and sometimes specific origin of the fiber, potentially connecting a suspect to a location or another piece of evidence.</skos:definition>
