        <rdfs:label>U.S. Executive Branch</rdfs:label>
        <skos:definition>The U.S. Executive Branch is the division of the federal government responsible for enforcing laws and administering public policy, headed by the President of the United States. It comprises the President, Vice President, Cabinet members, and federal agencies and departments.</skos:definition>
        <skos:prefLabel>Presidential Administration</skos:prefLabel>
    </owl:Class>
    


