        <skos:definition>A drug testing policy is a formal document established by an organization that outlines the procedures, guidelines, and consequences related to the testing of employees for the presence of drugs and/or alcohol. It generally seeks to ensure a safe and productive work environment by preventing substance abuse and its associated risks.</skos:definition>
    </owl:Class>
    


