        <skos:altLabel>Wealth Planning Practice</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:definition>Estate Planning Practice involves the preparation and arrangement of an individual&apos;s estate to manage and distribute assets during their lifetime and after death. It includes creating legal documents such as wills, trusts, and powers of attorney to ensure that an individual&apos;s wishes are followed and to minimize taxes and legal complications.</skos:definition>
