        <skos:definition>The Federal Emergency Management Agency (FEMA) is an agency of the United States Department of Homeland Security. The agency&apos;s primary purpose is to coordinate the response to a disaster that has occurred in the United States and that overwhelms the resources of local and state authorities.</skos:definition>
