        <rdfs:label>Chronic Myelogenous Leukemia</rdfs:label>
        <skos:definition>Chronic myelogenous leukemia (CML) is a type of cancer that originates in the bone marrow and leads to the uncontrolled growth of myeloid cells, characterized by the presence of the Philadelphia chromosome. It progresses slowly and can transform into a more aggressive form if not treated effectively.</skos:definition>
