        <skos:definition>A &quot;criminal legal determination&quot; pertains to the verdict or decision made by a court in a criminal case. It typically involves determining whether the defendant is found &quot;guilty&quot; or &quot;not guilty&quot; of the criminal charges brought against them. This determination has significant consequences, including potential penalties such as imprisonment, fines, probation, or other forms of punishment, depending on the verdict.</skos:definition>
