        <rdfs:label>D.V.M. (Doctor of Veterinary Medicine)</rdfs:label>
        <skos:altLabel>Doctor of Veterinary Medicine</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:definition>The suffix &quot;D.V.M.&quot; stands for &quot;Doctor of Veterinary Medicine&quot; and is used after a person&apos;s name to indicate that they have completed the educational and licensing requirements to practice veterinary medicine. This designation signifies the individual&apos;s credentials in animal healthcare and is commonly used in medical, academic, and professional settings.</skos:definition>
        <skos:prefLabel>D.V.M.</skos:prefLabel>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RB7SUFGYcCsVN2y5Rj7EvdI -->

