        <rdfs:label>En Banc</rdfs:label>
        <skos:definition>An en banc judicial filing refers to a legal submission to a court in which the case is heard before all judges of the court rather than by a panel of judges selected from them. This type of filing is typically reserved for complex cases or those of exceptional public importance, where a full court&apos;s review is deemed necessary to ensure a consistent and authoritative judicial decision.</skos:definition>
