        <dc:identifier>US-FD-TREAS-TIGTA</dc:identifier>
        <rdfs:label>Treasury Inspector General for Tax Administration</rdfs:label>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="fr-fr">Inspecteur général du Trésor pour l&apos;administration fiscale</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="es-es">Inspector General del Tesoro para la Administración Tributaria</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="es-mx">Inspector General del Tesoro para la Administración Tributaria</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="pt-br">Inspetor Geral do Tesouro para Administração Tributária</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="de-de">Schatzinspektorat für Steuerverwaltung</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en-gb">Treasury Inspector General for Tax Administration</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="he-il">מבקר האוצר הכללי למנהל המסים</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="hi-in">कर व्यवस्था के लिए ट्रेजरी इंस्पेक्टर जनरल</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="zh-cn">税务管理司库务检查总监</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="ja-jp">税務監督官事務局</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:definition>The Treasury Inspector General for Tax Administration (TIGTA) was established under the IRS Restructuring and Reform Act of 1998 to provide independent oversight of IRS activities. TIGTA promotes the economy, efficiency, and effectiveness in the administration of the internal revenue laws. It is also committed to the prevention and detection of fraud, waste, and abuse within the IRS and related entities.</skos:definition>
