        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RD3LBDAXqjURNXVGHaWXf7s"/>
        <rdfs:label>Patent Opposition Process</rdfs:label>
        <skos:definition>The patent opposition process is a legal procedure that allows third parties to challenge the validity of a patent or patent application. This process is intended to ensure that patents are only granted for inventions that meet the criteria of novelty, inventiveness, and industrial applicability.</skos:definition>
    </owl:Class>
    


