        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="de-de">Klausel zur Anpassung des Verbraucherpreisindex</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="he-il">סעיף התפתחות מדד מחירי הצרכן</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="hi-in">उपभोक्ता मूल्य सूचकांक वृद्धि शर्त</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="ja-jp">消費者物価指数エスカレーション条項</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="zh-cn">消费者价格指数升级条款</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:definition>A Consumer Price Index (CPI) Escalation Clause, also known as CPI, is a clause in a contract that allows for adjustments to be made to payments or prices based on changes in the CPI, which measures the average change in prices over time for goods and services consumed by households.</skos:definition>
    </owl:Class>
    


