        <rdfs:label>Insolvency Practice</rdfs:label>
        <skos:altLabel>Insolvencies</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel>Insolvency</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel>Insolvency Service</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:definition>Insolvency Practice encompasses the legal processes and procedures involved in handling the financial distress and liquidation of individuals and businesses unable to meet their debt obligations. It includes bankruptcy filings, debt restructuring, and the administration of insolvent estates. In the United Kingdom, insolvency is distinct from the U.S. concept of Bankruptcy.</skos:definition>
    </owl:Class>
    


