        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="de-de">Anspruch auf Schutz vor grausamer und ungewöhnlicher Bestrafung</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel>Cruel &amp; Unusual Punishment Clause Claim</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en-gb">Cruel and Unusual Punishment Claim</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="es-es">Reclamo de castigo cruel e inusual</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="es-mx">Reclamo de castigo cruel e inusual</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="pt-br">Reivindicação de proteção contra punições cruéis e incomuns</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="fr-fr">Revendication de protection contre les peines cruelles et inhabituelles</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="he-il">תביעה על עינויים אכזריים ובלתי רגילים</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="hi-in">निर्दयी और असामान्य दंड दावा</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="zh-cn">残忍和不寻常的惩罚索赔</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="ja-jp">残酷で異常な刑罰の主張</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:definition>A cruel and unusual punishment claim is a legal action initiated by an individual alleging that their Eighth Amendment right to be free from cruel and unusual punishment has been violated by the government or a government actor. The Eighth Amendment prohibits the government from imposing punishments that are excessive, torturous, or barbaric. A cruel and unusual punishment claim may arise in various contexts, such as when a person is subjected to excessive physical or mental pain, suffering, or humiliation during the course of their punishment, when a person is punished for a non-violent offense in a way that is disproportionate to the crime, or when a person is denied necessary medical treatment while in custody.</skos:definition>
    </owl:Class>
    


