        <skos:definition>The suffix &quot;R.N.&quot; stands for &quot;Registered Nurse&quot; and is used after a person&apos;s name to indicate that they are licensed to practice nursing. This designation confirms that the individual has met the educational and licensing requirements set forth by a nursing board or authority and is commonly used in healthcare settings, academic environments, and formal documents</skos:definition>
