        <skos:altLabel>Head of State Government</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel>State Executive</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel>Territorial Governmental Leader</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:definition>A State Governmental Leader is the highest-ranking official in a state, province, or similar sub-national administrative division. This individual is typically responsible for executing state laws, overseeing state agencies, proposing legislation, and representing the state&apos;s interests at both national and international levels.</skos:definition>
        <skos:prefLabel>Provincial Governmental Leader</skos:prefLabel>
    </owl:Class>
    


