        <rdfs:label>Biological Parent</rdfs:label>
        <skos:definition>A Biological Parent, also known as a birth parent, is an individual from whom a child inherits their genetic material. This refers to the mother, from whom a child is born, and the father, who contributes to the child&apos;s conception, distinguishing them from adoptive or step-parents.</skos:definition>
