        <skos:definition>Fiber crops are plants grown specifically for their fibers, which are used in the production of textiles, ropes, and other materials. These crops are cultivated for their natural fibers, which are harvested and processed into usable products for industrial and consumer purposes.</skos:definition>
        <skos:prefLabel>Textile Crops</skos:prefLabel>
    </owl:Class>
    


