    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RBdyeqVpZ95dzn6l0hQg3xE">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/Rd7uelGFqCTWSgf9lWki5N"/>
        <rdfs:label>Public Disclosure of Private Facts</rdfs:label>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="es-es">Divulgación pública de hechos privados</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="es-mx">Divulgación pública de hechos privados</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="fr-fr">Divulgation publique de faits privés</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="pt-br">Divulgação pública de fatos privados</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel>Doxxing</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en-gb">Public Disclosure of Private Facts</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="de-de">Öffentliche Offenlegung privater Fakten</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="he-il">חשיפה ציבורית של עובדות פרטיות</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="hi-in">निजी तथ्यों का सार्वजनिक खुलासा</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="zh-cn">公开披露私人事实</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="ja-jp">私的事実の公開</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:definition>The public disclosure of private facts is a type of privacy claim that involves the dissemination of personal information that is not of legitimate public concern, and that would be highly offensive to a reasonable person. This includes the practice of &quot;doxing&quot; (aka &quot;doxxing&quot;), which refers to the act of publicly revealing private or identifying information about an individual without their consent, typically with malicious intent. This information can include addresses, phone numbers, email addresses, or other personal details, and the practice is often associated with online harassment or cyberbullying.</skos:definition>
        <skos:prefLabel>Doxing</skos:prefLabel>
    </owl:Class>
    


