        <rdfs:label>Standstill Agreement</rdfs:label>
        <skos:definition>A Standstill Agreement is a contract in which one party agrees not to take specific actions against another party for a set period. It&apos;s often used in business contexts where one company agrees not to acquire more shares or make a takeover bid for another company for a specified duration.</skos:definition>
    </owl:Class>
    


