        <rdfs:label>Conditional Use Permit</rdfs:label>
        <skos:definition>A Conditional Use Permit is a type of land use authorization that allows a property owner to engage in activities not typically permitted within a specific zoning classification, subject to meeting predetermined conditions. This permit is granted by a local governing body after a review process, often involving public hearings and assessments.</skos:definition>
        <skos:prefLabel>Conditional Zoning Permit</skos:prefLabel>
    </owl:Class>
    


