        <rdfs:label>Law Review Article</rdfs:label>
        <skos:definition>A Law Review Article is a scholarly piece of writing published in a law review, which is a type of academic journal focused on legal and jurisprudential topics. These articles are written by legal scholars, practitioners, or law students, and they provide in-depth analysis, critique, or novel perspectives on legal theories, case law, statutes, or societal legal issues, often influencing legal thought and occasionally, policy or judicial decisions.</skos:definition>
    </owl:Class>
    


