        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="ja-jp">第6条請求</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:definition>An Article VI claim refers to a legal argument grounded in Article VI of the U.S. Constitution, which includes the Supremacy Clause, declaring federal laws and treaties to be the supreme law of the land. Such a claim may arise in disputes involving the precedence of federal law over state law, or the constitutionality of treaties.</skos:definition>
    </owl:Class>
    


