        <rdfs:label>Obligation of Contracts Clause Claim</rdfs:label>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="de-de">Anspruch aus der Klausel zur Verpflichtung von Verträgen</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en-gb">Obligation of Contracts Clause Claim</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="es-es">Reclamación de la Cláusula de Obligación de Contratos</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="es-mx">Reclamación de la Cláusula de Obligación de Contratos</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="pt-br">Reivindicação de cláusula de obrigação contratual</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="fr-fr">Réclamation de clause d&apos;obligation de contrat</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="he-il">תביעת סעיף החובה בחוזים</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="hi-in">अनुबंध शर्त दावा करना</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="zh-cn">合同义务条款索赔</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="ja-jp">契約義務条項請求</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:definition>An Obligation of Contracts Clause claim is a legal argument asserting that a law or government action violates the Obligation of Contracts Clause of the United States Constitution by impairing the obligations of existing contracts, without a legitimate public purpose, thereby infringing on the sanctity and enforceability of contractual rights.</skos:definition>
