        <rdfs:label>Entered a Location</rdfs:label>
        <skos:definition>&quot;Entered a Location&quot; refers to the act of a person or object crossing a geographic boundary to reside, conduct business, or exist within a jurisdiction. Examples include a person becoming a permanent resident of a state for tax purposes, an immigrant arriving in a destination country, or a product being imported into a country for trade purposes. These events often come with legal and regulatory implications.</skos:definition>
