        <rdfs:label>Paternity Test</rdfs:label>
        <skos:definition>A Paternity Test is a DNA test that compares the genetic material of an alleged father to that of a child to determine the likelihood of a biological relationship. This test is often used in legal contexts to establish parental rights, child support, or inheritance claims, but can also be used for personal reasons.</skos:definition>
    </owl:Class>
    


