        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="zh-cn">已售出货物的破产卖方</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:definition>An Insolvent Seller Having Sold Goods refers to a legal claim arising from a situation where a seller who is unable to pay their debts has sold goods to a buyer. This claim falls under the broader categories of Contract and Quasi-Contract Claims.</skos:definition>
    </owl:Class>
    


