        <skos:definition>The concept of &quot;Buyer Recovering Specifically Identified Goods&quot; refers to a legal claim made by a buyer against a seller for breach of contract, seeking to recover goods that were specifically identified in the contract and not delivered by the seller.</skos:definition>
