        <rdfs:label>Interval</rdfs:label>
        <skos:altLabel>Time Frame</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:definition>In legal contexts, an Interval refers to a specific duration or period between two points in time, often relevant in determining compliance, applicability, or effects of legal actions or provisions. It plays a critical role in statutes of limitations, compliance deadlines, and contractual obligations.</skos:definition>
