            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:label>Venture Capital Financing Documents</rdfs:label>
        <skos:definition>Venture Capital Financing Documents are a set of legal documents executed between venture capital firms and the businesses they are investing in. They detail the terms of the investment, the rights and obligations of each party, and often include provisions regarding the governance of the business, amongst other matters. These documents are related to the infusion of capital into a startup or growth-stage company in exchange for equity and other investment instruments, often as part of a series of such transactions, with the aim of accelerating business development and scaling operations.</skos:definition>
        <skos:prefLabel>VC Financing Documents</skos:prefLabel>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RCALpykvW6JoItA6jJjPT3G -->

