        <dc:source rdf:resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Single_non-transferable_vote"/>
        <rdfs:label>Single Non-Transferable Vote System</rdfs:label>
        <skos:altLabel>SNTV</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:definition>The Single Non-Transferable Vote (SNTV) system is an electoral method where each voter casts one vote for one candidate in a multi-member district, and the candidates with the highest number of votes win the seats. This system allows for minority representation by enabling voters to focus their support on a single candidate without the need for vote transfers.</skos:definition>
    </owl:Class>
    


