        <skos:definition>The concept of &quot;Obligor Aiding Agent Disloyalty to Principal&quot; refers to the legal liability of an agent who breaches their duty of loyalty to their principal by assisting an obligor in their efforts to harm the principal&apos;s interests.</skos:definition>
    </owl:Class>
    


