        <rdfs:comment>From LIST: Legal Issues Taxonomy — https://taxonomy.legal/</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Regulatory Processing Service</rdfs:label>
        <skos:definition>Regulatory processing service refers to legal services relating to administrative actions by governmental or regulatory bodies to review, assess, and process applications for various services or benefits (e.g., public benefits, intellectual property registration). This service involves steps like form submission, documentation verification, and legal review to determine an applicant&apos;s eligibility or the validity of a request, culminating in either approval, denial, or request for additional information</skos:definition>
    </owl:Class>
    


