        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="ja-jp">浪費家規定条項</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:definition>A spendthrift provision clause is a type of contractual clause that restricts a beneficiary&apos;s ability to transfer or assign their interest in a trust or estate, in order to protect the beneficiary&apos;s assets from creditors or other third parties.</skos:definition>
    </owl:Class>
    


