        <skos:definition>An &quot;Honorable Discharge&quot; from the military signifies that a service member has met or exceeded the conduct and performance standards of the armed forces throughout their service period. It indicates that the individual has served honorably, fulfilling their commitments effectively and without any significant disciplinary infractions.</skos:definition>
