        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="zh-cn">未成年人监护人</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="ja-jp">裁判所設置監護者</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:definition>A Guardian Ad Litem (GAL) is a court-appointed individual, often an attorney or a trained professional, who represents and protects the best interests of a minor, an incapacitated person, or someone otherwise unable to represent themselves in legal proceedings. The GAL investigates the circumstances of the case, communicates with relevant parties, and provides an independent report and recommendations to the court, ensuring that the person they represent receives fair and unbiased consideration of their needs and rights</skos:definition>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RCSG4k3ah1Pu5YgPexPgOmL -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RCSG4k3ah1Pu5YgPexPgOmL">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RDIwFaFcH4KY0gwEY0QlMTp"/>
        <dc:identifier>HTC</dc:identifier>
        <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="https://www.naics.com/six-digit-naics/?code=62"/>
        <rdfs:label>Health Care Industry</rdfs:label>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="de-de">Gesundheitswesen</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel>Health Care</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en-gb">Health Care Industry</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel>Healthcare Industry</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="es-es">Industria de la atención médica</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="es-mx">Industria de la atención médica</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="fr-fr">Industrie de la santé</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="pt-br">Indústria de cuidados de saúde</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="he-il">תעשיית טיפול בבריאות</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="hi-in">स्वास्थ्य देखभाल उद्योग</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="zh-cn">医疗保健行业</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="ja-jp">医療産業</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:definition>This industry group comprises establishments providing health care and social assistance for individuals. The sector includes both health care and social assistance.</skos:definition>
        <skos:hiddenLabel>HTC</skos:hiddenLabel>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RCSGK4INCgJwoB5OTwTpEFm -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RCSGK4INCgJwoB5OTwTpEFm">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RfP04tDTTpn4LDvwAxAqkh"/>
        <rdfs:label>Procedural Due Process Claim</rdfs:label>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="de-de">Anspruch auf ein faires Verfahren</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en-gb">Procedural Due Process Claim</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="es-es">Reclamación de debido proceso legal</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="es-mx">Reclamación de debido proceso legal</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="pt-br">Reivindicação de devido processo legal</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="fr-fr">Revendication de procédure régulière</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="he-il">תביעת תהליך דיון ראוי</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="hi-in">प्रक्रियात्मक योग्यता दावा</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="ja-jp">手続き上の正当な主張</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="zh-cn">程序正当性主张</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:definition>A procedural due process claim is a legal action initiated by an individual or entity alleging that their right to procedural due process, as protected by the Fifth and Fourteenth Amendments of the United States Constitution, has been violated by the government or a government actor. Procedural due process requires the government to follow fair and established procedures before depriving an individual of their life, liberty, or property interests. A procedural due process claim may arise in various contexts, such as when the government fails to provide adequate notice, a fair and impartial hearing, or an opportunity to be heard before taking an action that impacts an individual&apos;s rights. Examples of procedural due process violations include the termination of public benefits without prior notice, the suspension of a student from a public school without a hearing, or the seizure of property without proper procedures.</skos:definition>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RCSGUcPZ5uh2NokmVNXQbu3 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RCSGUcPZ5uh2NokmVNXQbu3">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RCDwLiS22z6MzQaQHS08hvk"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RtrxZGwgTL594abOAwpDkz"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#seeAlso"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/R97fVfsGrxXjdTlPquAgu6R"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:label>Freedom of Information Act Request</rdfs:label>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="de-de">Antrag nach dem Informationsfreiheitsgesetz</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="fr-fr">Demande en vertu de la loi sur la liberté d&apos;information</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en-gb">Freedom of Information Act Request</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="pt-br">Pedido de Acesso à Informação de acordo com a Lei de Liberdade de Informação</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="es-mx">Solicitud de la Ley de Acceso a la Información Pública</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="es-es">Solicitud de la Ley de Libertad de Información</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="he-il">בקשת חופש המידע על פי חוק</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="hi-in">सूचना की आज़ादी अधिनियम अनुरोध</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="zh-cn">信息自由法请求</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="ja-jp">情報公開請求</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:definition>A Freedom of Information Act (FOIA) Request is a formal request made under the FOIA law to obtain access to government records or information.</skos:definition>
        <skos:prefLabel>FOIA Request</skos:prefLabel>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RCSGywkPBv7f2ACrfTSiirV -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RCSGywkPBv7f2ACrfTSiirV">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RB4cFSLB4xvycDlKv73dOg6"/>
        <rdfs:label>PACER Nature of Suit Codes</rdfs:label>
        <skos:altLabel>NoS</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:definition>PACER Nature of Suit (NoS) Codes are a standardized set of codes used to categorize legal cases filed in the PACER system, with each code representing a specific type of legal claim or cause of action.</skos:definition>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RCSOFJGFjyBIx52S43z5Vzc -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RCSOFJGFjyBIx52S43z5Vzc">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RDmsvdtBrrw46UnCDJ0LKrJ"/>
        <rdfs:label>Writ</rdfs:label>
        <skos:definition>A writ is a formal written order issued by a body with administrative or judicial jurisdiction, often a court. Writs command the addressee to act or refrain from acting in some way, and they can take various forms such as writs of habeas corpus, mandamus, or certiorari.</skos:definition>
    </owl:Class>
    


