        <rdfs:label>Bankruptcy Schedule - Creditors Holding Claims Secured by Property</rdfs:label>
        <skos:altLabel>Collateralized Debt Schedule</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel>Insolvency Secured Creditors List</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel>Secured Claims Schedule</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel>Secured Creditors List</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel>Secured Debt Disclosure</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:definition>Bankruptcy Schedule - Creditors Holding Claims Secured by Property, also known as Schedule D, requires the debtor to list all creditors who have claims secured by the debtor&apos;s property. This schedule provides details about each secured claim, including the creditor&apos;s name, the amount owed, the collateral securing the debt, and the value of that collateral.</skos:definition>
