        <skos:definition>Pediatric Screening and Intervention Public Benefit refers to programs like the Early Periodic Screening, Diagnosis, and Treatment (EPSDT) Program in the U.S., which provides comprehensive healthcare services for children and adolescents. The program aims to identify and treat medical conditions early through regular screenings, diagnostic services, and treatment.</skos:definition>
