        <dc:source rdf:resource="https://www.ssa.gov/disability/professionals/bluebook/13.00-NeoplasticDiseases-Malignant-Adult.htm#13_05"/>
        <rdfs:label>Lymphoma</rdfs:label>
        <skos:altLabel>Lymphatic Cancer</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel>Lymphatic System Cancer</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel>Malignant Lymphoma</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:definition>Lymphoma is a type of cancer that originates in the lymphatic system, which includes the lymph nodes, spleen, thymus gland, and bone marrow. It encompasses various subtypes, including Hodgkin lymphoma and Non-Hodgkin lymphoma, with distinct characteristics and treatment approaches, but excludes T-cell lymphoblastic lymphoma.</skos:definition>
    </owl:Class>
    


