        <skos:definition>An Expiration Event in legal terms refers to the occurrence that triggers the end of a legal privilege (e.g., regulatory permission) or obligation (e.g., contract), rendering its terms no longer enforceable. It marks the conclusion of the legal permission or obligation.</skos:definition>
