        <skos:definition>A Cable Broadcast is the transmission of television content through coaxial or fiber-optic cables to subscribers, providing access to a wide range of channels and programming. This form of broadcasting offers both live and on-demand content, including news, entertainment, sports, and educational shows, delivered to viewers via a cable television service.</skos:definition>
