        <skos:altLabel>Cardiovascular Conditions</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel>Cardiovascular Diseases</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:definition>Cardiovascular disorders encompass any condition that impairs the normal functioning of the heart or the circulatory system, including arteries, veins, capillaries, and lymphatic vessels. These disorders can be congenital, present from birth, or acquired, developing over time due to various factors such as lifestyle or disease.</skos:definition>
        <skos:prefLabel>Heart and Circulatory Disorders</skos:prefLabel>
    </owl:Class>
    


