        <rdfs:label>Accounts Payable</rdfs:label>
        <skos:definition>Accounts Payable is an accounting term that represents a company&apos;s obligation to pay off short-term debts to its creditors or suppliers within a specified period. It appears on the balance sheet as a current liability and indicates the amounts that a company owes for goods or services received but not yet paid for.</skos:definition>
    </owl:Class>
    


