        <rdfs:label>Governmental Criminal Law Division</rdfs:label>
        <skos:altLabel>Criminal Justice Division</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel>District Attorney&apos;s Office</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel>Federal Prosecutor&apos;s Office</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel>Government Criminal Prosecution Office</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel>Prosecutor&apos;s Office</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel>Public Prosecutor&apos;s Office</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel>State Attorney&apos;s Office</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel>State Prosecutor&apos;s Office</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:definition>A Governmental Criminal Law Division is a government entity responsible for prosecuting criminal cases on behalf of the public. It conducts investigations, files charges, represents the government in criminal trials, and ensures the enforcement of criminal laws.</skos:definition>
    </owl:Class>
    


