        <skos:definition>A bankruptcy plan is a legal document that outlines the proposed financial restructuring or liquidation of a bankrupt entity, including the distribution of assets and repayment of debts, as required by the specific chapter of the bankruptcy code under which the entity is filing.</skos:definition>
