        <rdfs:label>Complicated Fracture of an Upper Limb</rdfs:label>
        <skos:definition>A non-healing or complex fracture of an upper extremity refers to a severe fracture of the arm or shoulder that fails to heal properly or involves complicated breaks that hinder the normal healing process. Such fractures may require advanced medical treatment due to complications such as misalignment, infection, or insufficient bone regeneration.</skos:definition>
