        <rdfs:label>Remedies in Property Law</rdfs:label>
        <skos:definition>Remedies in Property Law are legal actions or procedures used to enforce property rights and resolve disputes over property ownership or possession. Each remedy (e.g., foreclosure, seizure, attachment) serves to protect the interests of the property holder or creditor and is governed by specific laws and regulations.</skos:definition>
    </owl:Class>
    


