            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:label>Buyer In Breach Liable for Real Estate Broker&apos;s Commission</rdfs:label>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en-gb">Buyer In Breach Liable for Real Estate Broker&apos;s Commission</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="pt-br">Comprador em violação responsável pela comissão do corretor imobiliário</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="es-es">El comprador en incumplimiento es responsable de la comisión del corredor de bienes raíces</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="es-mx">El comprador en incumplimiento es responsable de la comisión del corredor de bienes raíces</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="de-de">Käufer bei Vertragsbruch haftbar für Maklerprovision im Immobilienbereich</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="fr-fr">L&apos;acheteur en violation est responsable de la commission du courtier immobilier</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="he-il">הקונה בהפרת החוזה אחראי על עמלת המתווך הנדלן</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="hi-in">खरीदार अनुपालन के लिए रियल एस्टेट ब्रोकर की आयोग देने के लिए उत्तरदायी होता है</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="ja-jp">不履行の買い手は不動産ブローカーの手数料に責任を負う</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="zh-cn">违约买方应对房地产经纪人佣金负责</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:definition>If a buyer fails to fulfill their obligations under a real estate contract, they may be held responsible for paying the commission owed to the broker who facilitated the sale.</skos:definition>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RDMlfBHhw2Mfk0FBrVCQJY9 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RDMlfBHhw2Mfk0FBrVCQJY9">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/R9uTFHGFCMBjtYw5MOmpotJ"/>
        <rdfs:label>Life Insurance Policy</rdfs:label>
        <skos:definition>A life insurance policy is a contract between an insurance company and a policyholder that provides a financial payout to designated beneficiaries upon the death of the insured individual. The policy often requires the payment of regular premiums in exchange for the death benefit, and may include other features like investment growth or cash value.</skos:definition>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RDMllTEq28i1rFUt6SWQz9y -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RDMllTEq28i1rFUt6SWQz9y">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/R3Q1HDu5jO8nvhdbr2Uj0c"/>
        <rdfs:label>Florida Circuit Court - Holmes County - 14th Circuit Court</rdfs:label>
        <skos:definition>A court located in Holmes County, Florida that is part of the larger Florida Circuit Court system.</skos:definition>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RDMmVnDBUmOnVx8i4ZpOt2G -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RDMmVnDBUmOnVx8i4ZpOt2G">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/R88D8i8AcSTUig2X3yPbFHg"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RcW4pUMnXuufMtnyvdX0dB"/>
        <rdfs:label>Escrow Agreement</rdfs:label>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="fr-fr">Accord de dépôt</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="es-es">Acuerdo de depósito en garantía</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="pt-br">Contrato de depósito</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="es-mx">Contrato de depósito en garantía</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en-gb">Escrow Agreement</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="de-de">Treuhandschaftsvereinbarung</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="he-il">הסכם אסקרו</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="hi-in">एस्क्रो समझौता</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="ja-jp">エスクロー契約</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="zh-cn">托管协议</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:definition>An Escrow Agreement is a legal contract between two parties where a third party holds and manages assets or funds until the conditions of the agreement are met.</skos:definition>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RDMmocc9Ine34BK9vSksb0k -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RDMmocc9Ine34BK9vSksb0k">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RCafxux1zDpXGZzqVBKNVpa"/>
        <rdfs:label>Trustworthy AI</rdfs:label>
        <skos:altLabel>Credible AI</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel>Dependable AI</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:definition>Trustworthy AI is an AI system characterized by three main components: (1) it must be lawful, ensuring compliance with all applicable laws and regulations, (2) it should be ethical, demonstrating respect for and adherence to ethical principles and values, and (3) it should be robust, both technically and socially, to prevent unintentional harm. Trustworthy AI concerns the trustworthiness of the AI system itself and includes all processes and actors involved in the AI system&apos;s life cycle, emphasizing respect for human rights and democratic values.</skos:definition>
        <skos:prefLabel>Reliable AI</skos:prefLabel>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RDMogej8AdNSlkztHiKlIGK -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RDMogej8AdNSlkztHiKlIGK">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/R9ce0e5pb4hAULGEtqlBCV8"/>
        <rdfs:comment>Stemmed from Bankruptcy Project</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Current Financial Obligations</rdfs:label>
        <skos:definition>Current Financial Obligations, also known as Current Liabilities, are debts or obligations that a company is expected to settle within one fiscal year or operating cycle, whichever is longer. These can include accounts payable, short-term loans, and other debts that are due within a short timeframe, and they are listed on a company&apos;s balance sheet.</skos:definition>
        <skos:prefLabel>Current Liability</skos:prefLabel>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RDMrBgmf7sx8XGaMk7zAnJ -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RDMrBgmf7sx8XGaMk7zAnJ">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/R3Q1HDu5jO8nvhdbr2Uj0c"/>
        <rdfs:label>Florida Circuit Court - Pinellas County - 6th Circuit Court</rdfs:label>
        <skos:definition>A court located in Pinellas County, Florida that is part of the larger Florida Circuit Court system.</skos:definition>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RDMvlybB2Ds3VpLsrk7GpCp -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RDMvlybB2Ds3VpLsrk7GpCp">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RB7BB00LuJawNLM8CZW6z7U"/>
        <rdfs:label>Mootness</rdfs:label>
        <skos:definition>Mootness refers to a legal principle where a case is deemed irrelevant because it no longer presents an ongoing issue, or the parties involved no longer have a legally recognizable interest in the outcome. When a case becomes moot, courts generally dismiss it, as there is no longer a &quot;live&quot; controversy to resolve</skos:definition>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RDN125qcdfOhqnuRT6midQw -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RDN125qcdfOhqnuRT6midQw">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RDpizZcACsM7yyhWpT5tJaM"/>
        <rdfs:label>Forward-looking MAE Standard - &quot;Could reasonably be expected to&quot; Language</rdfs:label>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="es-es">Estándar de MAE prospectivo - Lenguaje &quot;Podría esperarse razonablemente&quot;</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="es-mx">Estándar de MAE prospectivo - Lenguaje &quot;Podría esperarse razonablemente&quot;</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="de-de">Forward-Looking-MAE-Standard - Sprache &quot;Könnte vernünftigerweise erwartet werden&quot;</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en-gb">Forward-looking MAE Standard - &quot;Could reasonably be expected to&quot; Language</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="fr-fr">Norme Forward-Looking MAE - Langage &quot;Pourrait raisonnablement être attendu&quot;</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="pt-br">Padrão Forward-Looking MAE - Linguagem &quot;Poderia ser razoavelmente esperado&quot;</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="he-il">תקן MAE עתידני - שפת &quot;ניתן לצפות בצורה סבירה&quot;</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="hi-in">फॉरवर्ड-लुकिंग एमएई मानक - &quot;को तर्कसंगत रूप से उम्मीद किया जा सकता है&quot; भाषा</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="zh-cn">前瞻性 MAE 标准 - &quot;可以合理地预期&quot;</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="ja-jp">将来的な MAE 標準 - &quot;合理的に予想される可能性がある&quot; 言語</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:definition>A Forward-looking MAE Standard with &quot;Could reasonably be expected to&quot; Language is a legal concept that refers to a standard used in contracts to determine whether a particular event or circumstance could reasonably be expected to have a material adverse effect on a party&apos;s business, financial condition, or operations.</skos:definition>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RDN7998wQetdktQazmTXaYx -->

