        <rdfs:label>Trademark Cancellation Process</rdfs:label>
        <skos:definition>A trademark cancellation proceeding is a legal process in which a party seeks to remove an existing trademark registration from the official register. This proceeding can be initiated if the trademark is believed to be improperly registered or if it conflicts with a prior trademark.</skos:definition>
        <skos:prefLabel>Trademark Invalidity Action</skos:prefLabel>
    </owl:Class>
    


