        <skos:altLabel>EEA Region</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel>European Trade Region</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:definition>The EEA Market Region refers to the European Economic Area, which includes the member countries of the European Union (EU) and the European Free Trade Association (EFTA), except Switzerland. This region is characterized by the free movement of goods, services, capital, and people, facilitating a single market for businesses and consumers.</skos:definition>
        <skos:prefLabel>European Economic Area Market</skos:prefLabel>
    </owl:Class>
    


