        <skos:altLabel>Digital Fingerprint</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel>Document Checksum</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:definition>A hash identifier, also known as a document checksum, is a unique alphanumeric code generated by applying a cryptographic hash function to the content of a document or file. This identifier serves as a digital fingerprint, ensuring the integrity and authenticity of the document by allowing any alterations to be easily detected.</skos:definition>
        <skos:prefLabel>Document Hash</skos:prefLabel>
    </owl:Class>
    


