        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="ja-jp">相殺条項</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:definition>A right of set off clause is a provision in a contract that allows a party to offset or deduct a debt owed to them by the other party from any amount owed to that party under the same contract.</skos:definition>
    </owl:Class>
    


