            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:label>Prevailing Wage</rdfs:label>
        <skos:definition>The &quot;Prevailing Wage&quot; is the hourly wage, typically established by government authorities, that is paid to workers in a specific locality or industry for a particular type of labor. It is intended to ensure that workers on government-funded projects or in certain sectors receive a fair and competitive wage, often based on the average wage rates for similar work in the region.</skos:definition>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RDTQjBfa6Pz2zGqI91yBAbq -->

