        <rdfs:label>Life Estate</rdfs:label>
        <skos:definition>A Life Estate is a form of property ownership where an individual holds the rights to use, occupy, and benefit from a property for the duration of their life. Upon the individual&apos;s death, ownership of the property reverts back to the original owner or a designated remainderman, as stipulated in the life estate agreement</skos:definition>
    </owl:Class>
    


