        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RwipRpN2mP7u4u1N74MVzK"/>
        <rdfs:label>Interstate Commerce Clause Claim</rdfs:label>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="de-de">Anspruch aus dem Interstate Commerce Clause</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en-gb">Interstate Commerce Clause Claim</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="es-es">Reclamo de la Cláusula de Comercio Interestatal</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="es-mx">Reclamo de la Cláusula de Comercio Interestatal</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="pt-br">Reivindicação da Cláusula de Comércio Interestadual</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="fr-fr">Revendication de la clause de commerce inter-États</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="he-il">תביעת סעיף המסחר בין המדינות</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="hi-in">इंटरस्टेट वाणिज्य धारा दावा</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="ja-jp">州間商取引条項クレーム</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="zh-cn">州际商务条款索赔</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:definition>An Interstate Commerce Clause claim is a legal argument asserting that a state law or regulation violates the authority of the federal government to regulate commerce among the states. This claim is based on the interpretation that the Interstate Commerce Clause grants Congress the power to regulate trade and commerce that crosses state boundaries, thereby restricting state interference in this domain.</skos:definition>
    </owl:Class>
    


