        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="hi-in">क्वांटम मेरूट</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:definition>A claim for quantum meruit is a legal action seeking payment for the reasonable value of services or goods provided, when there is no contract or the contract is unenforceable, and is typically brought under the category of equitable relief or quasi-contract claims.</skos:definition>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RDYPEe8LDb2JFBgJwwqi7UT -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RDYPEe8LDb2JFBgJwwqi7UT">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RCBtDyjzrPbQyhvU5V64Irn"/>
        <rdfs:label>Company Constitution</rdfs:label>
        <skos:definition>A Company Constitution is a legal document that sets out the rules and regulations governing the internal management of a corporation. It is a comprehensive framework encompassing everything from director duties to shareholder rights.</skos:definition>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RDYQkIrF9BWPFhzJNbHSiE5 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RDYQkIrF9BWPFhzJNbHSiE5">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RC1ceWXE3emNHpYlrOvvmxG"/>
        <rdfs:label>The Southeastern Mvskoke Nation, Inc.</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RDYRWCSnEAUwPAZRo9iS6RV -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RDYRWCSnEAUwPAZRo9iS6RV">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/R7cIHUn7gvxaOltKIfA7Qta"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RCAIUgUHLdwFdtdPTruyEgL"/>
        <rdfs:label>Right of First Refusal Agreement</rdfs:label>
        <skos:altLabel>First Refusal Agreement</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel>Pre-emption Agreement</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel>ROFR</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel>ROFR Agreement</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:definition>A Right of First Refusal Agreement (ROFR) is a legal contract that grants a specified party the priority to purchase a particular asset before the owner is allowed to sell the asset to others. This agreement is often utilized in business ventures and real estate transactions to give existing stakeholders a chance to maintain their stake in the face of potential external interest.</skos:definition>
        <skos:definition>The Right of First Refusal and Co-Sale Agreement typically outlines the terms for the sale of an issuer&apos;s Preferred Stock to investors and defines obligations of certain, specified stockholders. It typically includes provisions for the Company&apos;s right of first refusal on transferable stock from specified stockholders, secondary purchase rights for stockholders, and specific notification timelines and conditions for stock transfers.</skos:definition>
    </owl:Class>
    


