        <rdfs:label>Community Property Claim</rdfs:label>
        <skos:altLabel>Communal Property Claim</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel>Conjugal Property Claim</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:definition>A community property claim relates to the legal concept of community property in certain jurisdictions. In divorce or dissolution of a marriage, community property refers to assets and debts acquired during the marriage that are considered jointly owned by both spouses. A community property claim involves asserting a legal right to an equitable division of these shared assets and liabilities between the divorcing parties</skos:definition>
        <skos:prefLabel>Marital Property Claim</skos:prefLabel>
    </owl:Class>
    


