        <rdfs:comment>From LIST: Legal Issues Taxonomy — https://taxonomy.legal/</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Nation-Provided Public Benefit</rdfs:label>
        <skos:definition>Nation-provided public benefit refers to social assistance programs that are administered and funded by a country&apos;s federal or national government. Examples include national healthcare systems, unemployment insurance, and pension schemes.</skos:definition>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RDcEbdiv7bBBmCCHnufifJp -->

