        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="zh-cn">名誉董事条款</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:definition>A Director Emeritus Clause is a provision in a contract that grants a former director of a company an honorary title and certain privileges, such as attending board meetings, without having any voting rights or responsibilities.</skos:definition>
    </owl:Class>
    


