        <rdfs:label>Investment Adviser Registration Document</rdfs:label>
        <skos:definition>An Investment Adviser Registration Document is a formal document filed with the country&apos;s financial regulator (e.g., U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission (SEC)) by investment advisers or other entities to register their services and provide essential information to the public and regulatory authorities. The document typically includes details about the entity&apos;s business practices, conflicts of interest, disciplinary information, and background of the principals.</skos:definition>
        <skos:prefLabel>Form ADV</skos:prefLabel>
    </owl:Class>
    


