        <rdfs:label>Leveraged Buyout</rdfs:label>
        <skos:definition>A Leveraged Buyout (LBO) is a financial transaction where a company is acquired primarily using borrowed funds, often by taking on substantial debt. The assets of the company being acquired, and often those of the acquiring company, are used as collateral for the loans.</skos:definition>
        <skos:note>We&apos;re still thinking through which parent this has.</skos:note>
        <skos:prefLabel>LBO</skos:prefLabel>
    </owl:Class>
    


