        <skos:definition>The Legal Aid Agency, formerly known as the Legal Services Commission, is an organization responsible for providing legal aid and ensuring that individuals who cannot afford legal representation have access to legal assistance. It oversees the funding and administration of legal aid services, promoting equal access to justice.</skos:definition>
        <skos:prefLabel>UK Legal Services Commission</skos:prefLabel>
    </owl:Class>
    


