        <rdfs:label>Child Support Guidelines</rdfs:label>
        <skos:definition>Child Support Guidelines are legal regulations or guidelines established by a government authority to determine the amount of financial support that a non-custodial parent is required to provide for their child or children. These guidelines take into account factors such as the parents&apos; incomes, the child&apos;s needs, and the cost of living. They provide a standardized method for calculating child support payments, ensuring fairness and consistency in support orders.</skos:definition>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RDrCoGiMIXR6TcVXppICUT5 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RDrCoGiMIXR6TcVXppICUT5">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/R9hR0S1zExtgPQTzV0LeyD3"/>
