        <rdfs:label>Monoplegia</rdfs:label>
        <skos:altLabel>Single-Limb Paralysis</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:definition>Monoplegia is the paralysis of a single limb or a specific region of the body, often resulting from nerve damage, brain injury, or neurological disorders. It typically affects either an arm or a leg and requires medical treatment and physical therapy to manage symptoms and improve functionality.</skos:definition>
        <skos:prefLabel>Localized Motor Impairment</skos:prefLabel>
    </owl:Class>
    


