        <skos:definition>The Bank&apos;s Wrongful Dishonor of Negotiable Instrument refers to the act of a bank refusing to pay a negotiable instrument, such as a check or promissory note, without a valid reason, resulting in damages to the party presenting the instrument.</skos:definition>
    </owl:Class>
    


