        <skos:altLabel>Basal Cell Cancer</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:definition>Basal cell carcinoma (BCC) is the most common type of skin cancer, originating in the basal cells found in the epidermis, the skin&apos;s outermost layer. It typically grows slowly and rarely metastasizes but can cause significant local damage if not treated, often requiring surgical excision or other localized treatments.</skos:definition>
