            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:label>Patent Registration Document</rdfs:label>
        <skos:definition>A Patent Registration Document is the official record issued by a patent office, such as the United States Patent and Trademark Office (USPTO), confirming the grant of a patent to an inventor for a specific invention. The document outlines the scope of protection afforded by the patent, including claims, drawings, and specifications, and serves as legal evidence of the inventor&apos;s exclusive rights to the invention for a set period.</skos:definition>
    </owl:Class>
    


