        <rdfs:label>Mollusks</rdfs:label>
        <skos:definition>Mollusks are a diverse phylum of invertebrate animals known as Mollusca, characterized by a soft body, which in many species is protected by a hard shell. This group includes snails, clams, squids, and octopuses, and they inhabit a wide range of environments from deep ocean floors to freshwater and terrestrial habitats.</skos:definition>
        <skos:prefLabel>Mollusca</skos:prefLabel>
    </owl:Class>
    


