        <dc:source>From LIST: Legal Issues Taxonomy — https://taxonomy.legal/</dc:source>
        <rdfs:label>Child Care Cost Claim</rdfs:label>
        <skos:definition>A Child Care Cost Claim is a request made by a parent or guardian to receive financial assistance or reimbursement for expenses related to the care of their child. This may include costs associated with daycare, after-school programs, or babysitters. Such claims are often made to government agencies or employers through childcare subsidy programs or flexible spending accounts.</skos:definition>
    </owl:Class>
    


