        <rdfs:label>Personality Disorder Discharge</rdfs:label>
        <skos:definition>A Military Personality Disorder Discharge refers to the release of a service member from active duty based on the diagnosis of a personality disorder that interferes with their ability to effectively serve in the military. This type of discharge is typically considered administrative and is based on the assessment that the disorder existed prior to service and was not a result of or aggravated by military duties.</skos:definition>
    </owl:Class>
    


