        <skos:altLabel>Employer-Provided Pension Plan</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel>Employer-Sponsored Pension Plan</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel>Work-Based Pension Plan</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:definition>A workplace-run pension account is a retirement savings plan provided and managed by an employer, often involving contributions from both the employer and the employee. These plans can include defined benefit plans, which promise a specified monthly benefit at retirement, and defined contribution plans, which depend on the amount contributed and the performance of the investments.</skos:definition>
        <skos:example>Pension Fund: CalPERS Pension Fund</skos:example>
    </owl:Class>
    


