        <rdfs:label>National Government Representative</rdfs:label>
        <skos:altLabel>Federal Government Officer</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel>National Elected Representative</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel>National-Level Public Official</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:definition>A National Government Representative is an elected or appointed official who serves at the highest level of a country&apos;s government, typically in the executive or legislative branch. This individual is responsible for making, debating, or executing national laws and policies, representing constituents or the nation as a whole, and participating in governance at the federal level.</skos:definition>
        <skos:prefLabel>Federal Official</skos:prefLabel>
    </owl:Class>
    


