        <skos:altLabel>Non-Malignant Intracranial Tumor</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:definition>A benign brain tumor is a non-cancerous growth in the brain that typically does not invade surrounding tissues or spread to other parts of the body. Despite being non-malignant, benign brain tumors can still cause significant health issues due to their location and pressure on surrounding brain structures, leading to symptoms such as headaches, seizures, and neurological deficits.</skos:definition>
        <skos:prefLabel>Non-Cancerous Brain Tumor</skos:prefLabel>
    </owl:Class>
    


