        <skos:definition>A design patent registration document is a legal certificate issued by a patent office that grants the holder exclusive rights to a unique visual design of a functional item for a certain period. It includes details about the design&apos;s appearance, such as shape, pattern, or ornamentation, and protects against unauthorized copying or imitation.</skos:definition>
