        <rdfs:label>Motion to Amend Schedules</rdfs:label>
        <skos:definition>A Motion to Amend Schedules is a formal request made in bankruptcy proceedings by a debtor seeking to modify previously filed schedules of assets, liabilities, income, expenses, or other financial statements. This motion is typically necessary when new information becomes available or errors are discovered in the original filings.</skos:definition>
