        <skos:definition>A Part-Time Employee is an individual who works fewer hours per week than what is considered full-time by their employer or by labor laws. While part-time employees may have more flexible schedules, they often have limited or no access to benefits like health insurance, retirement plans, and paid time off.</skos:definition>
    </owl:Class>
    


