        <rdfs:label>Term Sheet</rdfs:label>
        <skos:definition>A Term Sheet is a document that outlines the basic terms and conditions under which an investment or significant transaction will be made. It serves as a blueprint for subsequent, more detailed legal agreements. Term Sheets can be binding or non-binding and may include other, significant legal provisions such as non-complete language, no-shop clauses, liquidated damages, etc.</skos:definition>
    </owl:Class>
    


