        <skos:altLabel>Attachment of Earnings Order</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel>Earnings Attachment Order</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:definition>A Writ of Garnishment is a legal mechanism whereby a court orders a third party to withhold funds they owe to the debtor and to direct the payment to the creditor instead. It&apos;s commonly used to collect on a judgment by seizing wages, bank account funds, or other assets that are in the hands of someone other than the debtor.</skos:definition>
