        <skos:altLabel>Asset Appreciation Income</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel>Asset Sale Profits</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel>Capital Gains refer to the profit realized from the sale or exchange of an asset that has increased in value. This gain is the difference between the purchase price (or basis) of the asset and its selling price, and it is typically subject to taxation.</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel>Realized Gains</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel>Sale Proceeds</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:prefLabel>Investment Profits</skos:prefLabel>
    </owl:Class>
    


