        <rdfs:label>Sexual Orientation and Gender Identity Rights</rdfs:label>
        <skos:definition>Sexual Orientation and Gender Identity Rights refer to the legal and ethical protections aimed at ensuring individuals are not discriminated against based on their sexual orientation or gender identity. These rights may include freedom from persecution, equal employment opportunities, and access to healthcare and social services, and are increasingly recognized in international human rights law and national legislation.</skos:definition>
