        <rdfs:label>Approval from Prior Employer</rdfs:label>
        <skos:definition>Approval from a Prior Employer refers to an applicant&apos;s receipt of immigration petition approvals from a former employer, applicable to various applications. This approval indicates that the former employer had successfully sponsored the applicant for a specific visa or immigration status.</skos:definition>
        <skos:note>This tag is used in conjunction with other tags (e.g., I-140, I-129)</skos:note>
    </owl:Class>
    


