            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:label>Strict Liability</rdfs:label>
        <skos:definition>Strict liability refers to a legal doctrine where a party is held responsible for their actions or the consequences of those actions, regardless of intent or negligence. This means that the person or entity is liable for damages even if they didn&apos;t intend to cause harm or weren&apos;t negligent in their actions.</skos:definition>
    </owl:Class>
    


