        <rdfs:label>State Upper House Legislator</rdfs:label>
        <skos:altLabel>Member of State Senate</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:definition>A State Senator is an elected official who serves as a member of the upper chamber of a state&apos;s bicameral legislature. This individual is responsible for proposing, debating, and voting on state laws, policies, and budgets, as well as representing the interests of constituents from their specific senatorial district.</skos:definition>
        <skos:prefLabel>State Senator</skos:prefLabel>
    </owl:Class>
    


