        <skos:definition>A post-argument brief is a written document submitted to an appellate court after oral arguments have been made, providing additional legal arguments or clarifications to support the party&apos;s position.</skos:definition>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RgZ0caJ_nR16ICy4Ko3SOIg -->

