        <rdfs:label>Non-Hearsay Documents</rdfs:label>
        <skos:definition>Non-hearsay documents are written records that are admissible in court without the need for the author to testify, as they are considered exceptions to the hearsay rule. Examples include business records, public records, and learned treatises, which are deemed reliable due to their regular and official nature.</skos:definition>
