        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="ja-jp">従属条項</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:definition>A subordination clause is a provision in a contract that places one obligation or agreement below another in priority, typically used in real estate transactions to subordinate a lease to a mortgage.</skos:definition>
    </owl:Class>
    


