        <rdfs:label>Hemolytic Anemias</rdfs:label>
        <skos:definition>Hemolytic Anemias are a group of conditions characterized by the premature destruction of red blood cells, leading to a decreased number of circulating red blood cells and a resultant anemia. The condition can be caused by intrinsic factors, such as genetic defects, or extrinsic factors, such as autoimmune reactions or infections.</skos:definition>
    </owl:Class>
    


