        <skos:definition>A Certificate of Limited Partnership is a legal document filed with a state&apos;s Secretary of State or similar government agency to officially register a limited partnership (LP). It typically includes information such as the partnership&apos;s name, purpose, registered agent, and the names of its general and limited partners.</skos:definition>
