        <skos:definition>Authorship, particularly human authorship in copyright law, designates the creation of a work by a human being, attributing legal rights and responsibilities to the creator. This principle recognizes the human creator as the source of intellectual creativity and grants them exclusive rights over their work.</skos:definition>
