        <skos:altLabel>National Assembly Member</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel>National-Level Legislative Representative</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:definition>A National Legislator is an elected or appointed official who serves as a member of a country&apos;s national law-making body. This individual is responsible for proposing, debating, and voting on national laws and policies, representing constituents or regions at the federal level, and providing oversight of the executive branch.</skos:definition>
        <skos:prefLabel>Federal Lawmaker</skos:prefLabel>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RmbIWgczQaXs5xSsXa4Zod -->

