        <rdfs:label>Bankruptcy Schedule - Creditors with Unsecured Claims</rdfs:label>
        <skos:altLabel>Insolvency Unsecured Creditors List</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel>Non-Secured Debt Schedule</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel>Schedule F</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel>Unsecured Claims Schedule</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel>Unsecured Creditors List</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel>Unsecured Debt Disclosure</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:definition>Bankruptcy Schedule - Creditors with Unsecured Claims, also known as Schedule E/F, requires the debtor to list all creditors who hold unsecured claims against them. This schedule distinguishes between priority unsecured claims, which have a higher repayment priority under bankruptcy law, and non-priority unsecured claims, detailing the creditor&apos;s name, claim amount, and the nature of the claim.</skos:definition>
        <skos:prefLabel>Schedule E</skos:prefLabel>
    </owl:Class>
    


