        <rdfs:label>Board of Zoning Appeals</rdfs:label>
        <skos:altLabel>Land Use Appeals Board</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel>Land Use Regulatory Appeals Body</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel>Variance Appeals Committee</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel>Zoning Adjustment Board</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:definition>The Board of Zoning Appeals (BZA) is a specialized governmental body that hears and decides upon appeals, variances, and special exceptions related to local zoning ordinances. Typically quasi-judicial in nature, the BZA reviews cases where applicants seek relief from or challenge the strict application of zoning regulations.</skos:definition>
