        <skos:definition>This claim arises when digital content or services, such as websites, mobile apps, or other online platforms, are not designed or structured to be accessible to individuals with disabilities. This can include issues like lack of screen reader compatibility, missing alternative text for images, or inaccessible video content.</skos:definition>
