        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="ja-jp">第3条請求</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:definition>An Article III claim pertains to a legal argument based on Article III of the U.S. Constitution, which establishes the judicial branch of the federal government. Such a claim may arise in disputes over federal court jurisdiction, the interpretation of federal laws, or the constitutionality of legislation or executive actions.</skos:definition>
