        <skos:altLabel>Dual-Use Export Violation Claim</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel>EAR Violation Claim</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:definition>An EAR Claim arises when an individual or entity violates the Export Administration Regulations, which govern the export and re-export of dual-use items, software, and technology from the United States. This claim involves allegations of unauthorized export, re-export, or transfer of items subject to EAR to prohibited destinations, entities, or individuals.</skos:definition>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RsTnyZoBckeYgjbwks7DL8 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RsTnyZoBckeYgjbwks7DL8">
