        <dc:source rdf:resource="https://www.ssa.gov/disability/professionals/bluebook/13.00-NeoplasticDiseases-Malignant-Adult.htm#13_14"/>
        <rdfs:label>Lung Cancer</rdfs:label>
        <skos:altLabel>Lung Carcinoma</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel>Pulmonary Carcinoma</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:definition>Lung cancer is a type of cancer that begins in the lungs, often in the cells lining the air passages. It can be classified into different types, primarily non-small cell lung cancer (NSCLC) and small cell lung cancer (SCLC), each requiring specific treatments such as surgery, chemotherapy, radiation therapy, and targeted therapy.</skos:definition>
    </owl:Class>
    


