        <skos:definition>Business formation practice refers to the legal service in which lawyers assist individuals in establishing a new business, covering aspects like selecting the appropriate business structure, filing necessary paperwork, and ensuring compliance with local, state, and federal regulations. Lawyers in this field guide clients through legal complexities to mitigate risk and create a sound legal foundation for the business</skos:definition>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RvpY1fp6IX31yViO9GQMkq -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RvpY1fp6IX31yViO9GQMkq">
