        <rdfs:label>Radishes</rdfs:label>
        <skos:altLabel>Raphanus Sativus</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:definition>Radishes are edible root vegetables belonging to the Raphanus sativus species, characterized by their crisp texture and pungent flavor. They are typically small, round or elongated in shape, with colors ranging from white to red to black, and are consumed raw in salads, as garnishes, or cooked in various culinary applications.</skos:definition>
    </owl:Class>
    


