        <skos:altLabel>Master of Business Administration</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:definition>The suffix &quot;M.B.A.&quot; stands for &quot;Master of Business Administration&quot; and is used after a person&apos;s name to indicate that they have earned an advanced degree in business management. This designation signifies the individual&apos;s expertise in various aspects of business, such as finance, marketing, and operations, and is commonly used in professional, academic, and formal settings</skos:definition>
        <skos:prefLabel>M.B.A.</skos:prefLabel>
    </owl:Class>
    


