            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:label>Occupancy</rdfs:label>
        <skos:definition>Occupancy refers to the act of residing in or using a property or space. This includes the possession and control of the property, typically under a lease or ownership agreement, and entails responsibilities such as maintenance and adherence to property regulations. Occupancy refers to the physical act of living in or using a property, which can be temporary or intermittent, in contrast to &quot;residence,&quot; which refers to a person&apos;s fixed, permanent, and principal home, often with legal implications and the intention to remain for an extended period.</skos:definition>
        <skos:prefLabel>Property Use</skos:prefLabel>
    </owl:Class>
    


