        <skos:altLabel>North American Trade Region</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:definition>The NAFTA Market Region encompasses the countries that were part of the North American Free Trade Agreement—Canada, the United States, and Mexico—characterized by integrated supply chains, significant trade flows, and economic collaboration. This region is known for its extensive cross-border trade and investment, driven by the harmonization of regulations and the reduction of trade barriers.</skos:definition>
