        <skos:definition>The &quot;Right to Effective Assistance of Counsel&quot; refers to an individual&apos;s entitlement not only to legal representation but to representation that is competent and effective. It means that a lawyer must perform adequately and any significant failure in this duty can lead to a violation of a defendant&apos;s rights, potentially resulting in reversals of convictions or other legal remedies.</skos:definition>
    </owl:Class>
    


