        <rdfs:label>Wet Corn Milling and Starch Manufacturing</rdfs:label>
        <skos:definition>This U.S. industry comprises establishments primarily engaged in wet milling corn and other vegetables (except to make ethyl alcohol). Examples of products made in these establishments are corn sweeteners, such as glucose, dextrose, and fructose; corn oil; and starches (except laundry).</skos:definition>
    </owl:Class>
    


