    <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/R76moTYI55jCUBnHVsRVU87">
        <skos:definition>In project management, a person who is responsible for completing tasks.</skos:definition>
    </rdf:Description>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/R7JOAs1Mr9l4EMJPDttl21O">
        <skos:definition>In project management, a person who delegates work and reviews deliverables.</skos:definition>
    </rdf:Description>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/R7PEVL4EDe99UD7dVx58cFp">
        <skos:prefLabel>retained</skos:prefLabel>
        <rdfs:label>engaged</rdfs:label>
        <skos:definition>E.g., Client folio:engaged Lawyer</skos:definition>
        <owl:inverseOf>folio:isEngagedBy</owl:inverseOf>
        <skos:definition>E.g., Lawyer folio:engaged Expert</skos:definition>
        <skos:altLabel>retained</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel>engaged</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:notation>folio:hired</skos:notation>
        <skos:altLabel>hired</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:notation>folio:engaged</skos:notation>
        <skos:notation>folio:retained</skos:notation>
        <skos:definition>In a legal and contractual context, &quot;engaged&quot; refers to the act of formally hiring or retaining a professional, such as a lawyer, expert, or contractor, to perform specific services. This involves entering into a professional relationship, often governed by a contract or agreement, where the engaged party agrees to provide their expertise or services in exchange for compensation or other terms.</skos:definition>
    </rdf:Description>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/R7vNJkQAsTzqgVpEJ15NjNR">
        <rdfs:label>DELETE ME SDNY</rdfs:label>
    </rdf:Description>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/R8HkzaI7mhxBrouTHP3Erfr">
        <rdfs:label>ZZZ Motion to Dismiss</rdfs:label>
    </rdf:Description>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/R9e8PXI2IEusTTC9xKXN7hA">
        <skos:example>Contractual Party A is adverse to Contractual Party B</skos:example>
        <skos:example>Plaintiff is adverse to Defendant</skos:example>
        <skos:altLabel>is adverse to</skos:altLabel>
        <rdfs:label>isAdverseTo</rdfs:label>
        <skos:notation>folio:isAdverseTo</skos:notation>
        <skos:definition>In legal terminology, &quot;is adverse to&quot; describes a relationship characterized by opposition, conflict, or differing interests between parties in a legal context. This typically applies to situations where one party&apos;s interests, claims, or actions are directly opposed to those of another party, as in litigation, contractual disputes, or criminal proceedings.</skos:definition>
    </rdf:Description>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RBCRuVST523smryfQLOV3F1">
        <skos:definition>In project management, a person who is informed about a project&apos;s progress.</skos:definition>
    </rdf:Description>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RM0twdYxnRn6AgVaadoKYF">
        <skos:definition>In project management, a person who provides suggestions on how the project will impact their domain of expertise.</skos:definition>
    </rdf:Description>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RTVHIHUY48KidG92GXtTlH">
        <skos:definition>In corporate law and business, &quot;has subsidiary&quot; refers to the relationship where a parent company owns and controls a separate and distinct company, known as a subsidiary. This denotes that the subsidiary operates as an independent entity but is under the significant influence or control of the parent corporation, both in management and often in financial matters.</skos:definition>
        <skos:example>Meta hasSubsidiary Facebook</skos:example>
        <skos:example>Alphabet hasSubsidiary Google</skos:example>
        <skos:altLabel>has the subsidiary</skos:altLabel>
        <rdfs:label>hasSubsidiary</rdfs:label>
        <skos:notation>folio:hasSubsidiary</skos:notation>
    </rdf:Description>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/Ra83qMFRc1eaXroDluykqR">
        <rdfs:label>DELETE ME ND CAL</rdfs:label>
    </rdf:Description>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#seeAlso">
